 which is still going:\n\n**Implemented** (worktree `.temp/TASK-260822-b0wg3a/worktree`, branch `task/TASK-260822-b0wg3a-install-precheck` off `origin/main` 6a9b201):\n\n- `internal/install/buildsshcandidates.go` — discovery of the live agent (key count via `ssh-add -l`, degrading to \"unavailable\" on every failure except exit 1, which is a real \"agent holds nothing\" answer) and `~/.ssh/*.pub`, capped at 8 with the remainder counted. Builds the ready-to-run `curator config build-ssh add` commands.\n- `internal/install/buildsshprompt.go` — two-question flow (credential, then scope), default entry is the agent **pinned** to the first key, `m` for a manual path, `q`/EOF aborts with `build_repository_ssh_credential_missing`. `persist` is only reached after both answers.\n- `resolveBuildSSH` runs before the first fetch and names *every* uncovered repository at once; non-interactive fails closed with candidate-built commands.\n- The resolver is gated on `term.IsTerminal` for both stdin and stderr, and never supplied on a dry run.\n\n**One change to predecessor code:** the `plan.messages → Result.Messages` hop was duplicated in `install.go` and `global.go` with no test — a dropped loop would have left the suite green while the operator saw no dry-run provenance. Extracted as `externalPlan.credentialReport(label)` and covered.\n\n**Gates run standalone, real exit codes:**\n\n| Command | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `go build ./...` | exit 0 |\n| `go vet ./...` | exit 0 |\n| `gofmt -l .` | no output |\n| `golangci-lint run ./...` (v2.12.2) | `0 issues.`, exit 0 |\n| `.github/ci/gate-selftest.sh` | 75 passed, 0 failed, exit 0 |\n| 40 named buildssh/prompt/precheck/candidate tests | all PASS, exit 0 |\n| `go test -count=1 -timeout 30m ./...` | **still running** |\n\nTwo things worth flagging now:\n\n- **The `cmd/curator` suite is not hanging.** It needs ~10 minutes (`godriver` fingerprints the whole GOROOT); at `-timeout 5m` it panics with a stack in `digestToolchainRecords` and reads exactly like a deadlock. Cost me two wasted runs. Logged, and saved to memory.\n- **A sharp edge I left in deliberately:** discovery lists `*.pub` files as the task specifies. That is correct for the default agent-pinned entry (`-i key.pub` is exactly how you pin an agent), but the agent-less \"identity `<key>.pub`\" menu entry produces a selection that cannot authenticate — nothing validates that an identity path is a usable private key. Narrowing it is a product call about what discovery may read from `~/.ssh`, not a bug in this precheck, so I documented it for the docs task rather than changing behaviour.\n\nNine of ten checklist items are checked; \"dry-run reports per-repository credential source; go test green\" stays unchecked until the suite actually exits 0, and I'll hand off to review once it does.","ttft_ms":2097,"ttft_stream_ms":1348,"time_to_request_ms":40,"type":"result","duration_ms":2475459,"uuid":"6a46ba12-fd53-48dc-a6cb-7357a0f4df15"}
